Hash: SHA512

annotations:
  artifacthub.io/category: storage
  artifacthub.io/changes: |
    - kind: fixed
      description: Node plugin now bidirectionally mounts the entire kubelet root (default /var/lib/kubelet) instead of just /var/lib/kubelet/pods. Previously the per-volume staging directory (plugins/kubernetes.io/csi/<driver>/<volHandle>/globalmount) was created and mounted inside the container's ephemeral overlayfs, so a node-plugin pod restart (rolling update, OOM, image pull, crashloop) wiped the staging mount. Kubelet's actualStateOfWorld still believed the volume was staged and called NodePublishVolume directly, which then failed with "bind-mount: special device .../globalmount does not exist" — pods stuck ContainerCreating, eviction cascades. With the bidirectional mount the staging mount lives on the host and survives plugin restarts.
    - kind: added
      description: Helm chart packages are now GPG-signed. CI runs `helm package --sign` and publishes the `.prov` provenance file alongside the `.tgz`, plus the public key at /key.gpg. Verify with `helm install --verify`. Artifact Hub picks up the "Signed" badge automatically.
    - kind: added
      description: Online volume resize. ControllerExpandVolume calls E2E's PUT /block_storage/{id}/vm/upgrade/ (the API E2E enabled for us in May 2026); NodeExpandVolume grows ext4/xfs in-place via mount-utils. csi-resizer sidecar is back in the controller Deployment with --handle-volume-inuse-error=false (online resize) and --timeout=120s (covers the ~15-20s OpenNebula resize lag, plus HOTPLUG retry on freshly-attached volumes). RBAC adds pods get/list/watch for csi-resizer.
    - kind: changed
      description: storageClass.allowVolumeExpansion default flipped back to true now that resize is implemented. Existing installs unaffected — Kubernetes lets you flip allowVolumeExpansion on a StorageClass at any time.
    - kind: added
      description: values.schema.json — Helm now validates user values on install/upgrade/template/lint, and ArtifactHub renders the schema panel on the chart page. Enforces anyOf(inline e2e creds OR existingSecret), enum constraints on image.pullPolicy / storageClass.reclaimPolicy / storageClass.parameters.fsType, and integer-string IOPS.
    - kind: fixed
      description: NodeStageVolume now identifies the freshly attached disk by picking the unmounted virtio device with the highest diskseq, instead of diffing /sys/block before/after a PCI rescan. The diff approach was racy — by the time NodeStage runs, the device is often already enumerated by the kernel, so the diff returned empty and the driver gave up with "no new block device appeared within 30s after attach". Reads /host/proc/1/mounts (host PID-1's mount NS) to identify which devices are already in use.
    - kind: fixed
      description: NodeStageVolume is now idempotent — if the staging path is already mounted, returns success instead of re-running device discovery
    - kind: fixed
      description: DetachVolume now considers "attached to a different VM" as success for the requested target VM. CSI sometimes leaves a stale per-node VolumeAttachment after a cross-node move; reconciling that VA was waiting for status=Available which never arrives because the volume is happily attached elsewhere, leaving the PV in a permanent Released state with detach errors.
    - kind: fixed
      description: DetachVolume treats HTTP 412 "Disk is not attached to vm" as success (CSI retries detach idempotently; the old behavior wedged VolumeAttachment objects on cross-node move)
    - kind: changed
      description: AttachVolume / DetachVolume polls tightened to 1s with shorter caps (60s precheck, 30s post-attach) so the create→attach path lands in ~10–15s instead of 30–60s
    - kind: fixed
      description: Node plugin reads /host/sys/block instead of /sys/block — containerd remounts /sys per-container so the chart's hostPath:/sys was being shadowed and the post-attach device-discovery diff always returned no new device
    - kind: fixed
      description: AttachVolume now polls for status=Available before issuing the PUT, eliminating the HTTP 500 retry loop ControllerPublishVolume hit when CreateVolume returned status=Creating
    - kind: removed
      description: csi-resizer sidecar (E2E API does not expose volume resize for non-admin tokens; the role required for PATCH /block_storage/{id}/ is gated)
    - kind: changed
      description: Default image.tag is now `latest` with imagePullPolicy Always; pin to a numeric tag for reproducible deploys
    - kind: changed
      description: storageClass.allowVolumeExpansion default flipped to false to match the no-resizer reality
    - kind: fixed
      description: Driver renamed to csi.e2enetworks.com (vendor-namespaced)
    - kind: fixed
      description: Controller binary registers Node CSI service so sidecar capability probes succeed
    - kind: added
      description: Initial release with CreateVolume / DeleteVolume / Attach / Detach / Stage / Publish
    - kind: added
      description: Single-binary controller + node plugin
    - kind: added
      description: Helm chart with controller Deployment, node DaemonSet, RBAC, CSIDriver, StorageClass
